{"objective":"Deliver the MVP defined by walkie/scp:mvp-text-voicenote: text messaging, server-authoritative presence, and asynchronous push-to-talk voice notes, on builds that work across the whole device fleet.\n\nThis container covers phase 0 and phase 1 of walkie/plan:roadmap-v1. Phase 0 is a single blocking spike on the audio toolchain; its failure has a defined consequence — the voice-note item leaves the container and the MVP ships as text and presence only.\n\nThe container is created in state `planned`. Activation is deliberately NOT performed here: activating it locks walkie/plan:roadmap-v1 to immutable, and that belongs to execution, not to planning.","workItems":"Sixteen items, grouped by the order they unblock each other. This prose is descriptive only — actual membership is carried by the tkt- units that derive from both this container and their work item.\n\n**Blocking spike.** spk:audio-toolchain-viability — must complete before sto:voice-note starts.\n\n**Foundation.** ts:protocol-schema-v1, ts:coordinator-skeleton, ts:test-harness. These gate almost everything else: the schema defines the wire, the coordinator provides the endpoint, and the harness makes reconnect and queue behaviour testable rather than hand-verified.\n\n**Core features.** sto:text-messaging, sto:message-history, sto:device-presence, sto:offline-queue, ts:reconnect-resume.\n\n**Security.** ts:queue-sealed-box — depends on the offline queue existing, since it encrypts what the queue stores.\n\n**Voice.** sto:voice-note — gated on the spike.\n\n**Surface.** sto:terminal-ui, ts:control-socket.\n\n**Delivery and operability.** ts:build-release-matrix, ts:observability-baseline, ts:docs-quickstart-runbook.","changeLog":"Created 2026-08-20 in state planned, during the initial walkie planning session, deriving from the approved plan walkie/plan:roadmap-v1. No activation performed."}